name: "jaildeck"
version: "%%VERSION%%"
origin: "sysutils/jaildeck"
comment: "FreeBSD jail operations dashboard and host agent"
desc: "Jail Deck manages FreeBSD jails through native system tools, with a JSON API and an embedded Svelte web interface. Configuration, credentials, audit history and ZFS resources remain operator-owned."
maintainer: "andreluiscunha81@gmail.com"
www: "https://github.com/ottermq/jaildeck"
prefix: "/usr/local"
abi: "%%ABI%%"
licenselogic: "single"
licenses: ["MIT"]
categories: ["sysutils"]
messages: [{
    type: "install"
    message: <<EOD
Jail Deck has not been configured, initialized, enabled or started.

As root, for a new installation only:
  cp -n /usr/local/etc/jaildeck/jaildeck.env.sample /usr/local/etc/jaildeck/jaildeck.env
  vi /usr/local/etc/jaildeck/jaildeck.env
  set -a; . /usr/local/etc/jaildeck/jaildeck.env; set +a
  jaildeck passwd
  sysrc jaildeck_enable=YES
  service jaildeck start

Review host readiness before explicitly running jaildeck init. The package
does not create ZFS datasets or change networking. Credentials, tokens, logs,
live configuration and jail datasets are never package-owned.

Build and lifecycle documentation:
  https://github.com/ottermq/jaildeck/blob/dev/docs/PACKAGING.md
EOD
}]
